---
title: Crispy roast potatoes
servings: 8
tags: [vegan, holiday]
time: 1 hour 25 minutes
source: The Best Crispy Roast Potatoes Ever by J. Kenji López-Alt, Serious Eats, https://www.seriouseats.com/the-best-roast-potatoes-ever-recipe
---

Heat the oven to 450°F (230°C), or 400°F (200°C) on convection, with a rack in
the middle.

Bring @water{2%l} to a boil in a #large pot{}. Add @kosher salt{2%tbsp}, the
@baking soda{1/2%tsp} and the
@russet potatoes{4%lb}(peeled and cut into large chunks). Return to a boil, then
simmer ~{10%minutes}, until a knife slides in with little resistance.

While they cook, warm the @extra-virgin olive oil{5%tbsp} in a #small saucepan{}
over medium heat with the @fresh rosemary{}(a small handful, finely chopped),
the @garlic{3%cloves}(minced) and a few grinds of @black pepper{}. Stir and
shake ~{3%minutes}, just until the garlic starts to turn golden, then pour it
straight through a #fine-mesh strainer{} into a #large bowl{}. Keep the garlic
and rosemary aside.

Drain the potatoes and leave them in the pot ~{30%seconds} to steam dry. Tip
them into the oil, season with a little more salt and pepper, and shake the bowl
hard until the chunks are coated in a thick, mashed-looking paste.

Spread them out on a #large rimmed baking sheet{} and roast ~{20%minutes}
without touching them. Loosen any that stick with a thin metal spatula, shake
the pan and turn them.

Roast another ~{30%minutes} to 40 minutes, turning and shaking a few times,
until deep brown and crisp all over.

Toss in a bowl with the fried garlic and rosemary and the
@fresh parsley{}(a small handful, minced). Season to taste and serve at once.

> Duck fat, goose fat or beef fat can stand in for the olive oil. Yukon Gold
> potatoes work too. The baking soda roughs up the surface, which is what makes
> the crust.
